@echo-125/deh-remote README · Requirements：- A DSH installation whose `dsh` CLI supports profiles (`dsh --profile`, `dsh plugin`) — the profile/bundle mechanism this package rides on.
- For LAN use, either flip the **局域网访问** toggle in the settings card — it listens at once on this machine's current LAN IPv4 address at the web server's port, so after a network change flip it off and on again — or start with `dsh web --host <a LAN address of this machine>`. A wildcard `--host 0.0.0.0` works only on a host that still accepts it; DSH 0.2.1-rc.2 and later refuses it outright. With the default `127.0.0.1` bind and the toggle off the panel shows an explicit explanation instead of a dead QR code. The panel's mint/stop endpoints are loopback-only by design: a desktop browser opened at the LAN URL sees a "配对面板仅限本机使用" banner.
- The host firewall rule needs administrator rights: Windows and Linux are managed by the plugin (netsh, firewalld, ufw, iptables), while macOS and platforms with no supported manager report the firewall as unmanaged and normally need no rule. A refused rule is reported and leaves the loopback listener untouched.

@echo-125/deh-remote README · Or from this checkout (development loop)：dsh plugin --profile web add link:$(pwd)
```

Restart the profile (`dsh web`), then open the phone icon in the sidebar foot. The plugin's `cordis.patch.yml` inserts the single plugin row that mounts both halves.

@echo-125/deh-remote README · Or from this checkout (development loop)：> `github:<org>/<repo>` installs work because the package sits at this repo's root (the `prepare` script builds `lib/` during install; pnpm ≥10 blocks that until you copy the printed key into the profile's `pnpm-workspace.yaml` `allowBuilds` and re-run).
>
> The bundle must also be listed in the profile's `dsh.profile.bundles`. A dependency alone is not enough: the plugin-manager composes the bundle's patch only for bundles that list declares, and without it the plugin never loads at all (its routes answer 404 and no settings surface appears).

@echo-125/deh-remote README · Use：1. Open the settings card (单独安装时在 设置 → 插件 → 本插件行；全家桶安装时在 设置 → Web 插件 → 远程访问) and flip **局域网访问** on; the card shows the live bind, the forwarder state beside the host's own `localBindHost`, the firewall state, and the reachable LAN URLs, and it says why the LAN entry is off when this machine has no LAN address. The forwarder starts and stops at once, with no restart: after a network change, flip the toggle off and on again so it follows the machine's new address.
2. Start `dsh web`, click the phone icon, and the panel mints a fresh time-limited QR.
3. Scan with the phone (or open the copied link): the device pairs and boots the **official Web GUI** served cookieless by the plugin (`/pair-accept` → `/pair-app?grant=...`), which reloads into `/` on an https origin, or keeps `/pair-app` in the address bar over plain-HTTP LAN. On a multi-homed machine the landing may switch the phone to another advertised LAN candidate that answers `/pair-ping`, carrying a fresh one-time grant; a phone that reaches none simply stays on the page it was served. On a phone, the portrait adaptation layer is already active — same layout as the desktop, same live state. Later

@echo-125/deh-remote README · Manual E2E: LAN pairing round trip：1. Start an isolated instance: `DSH_HOME=/tmp/dsh-qa dsh --profile web --no-open --port 3191`; open the card at `http://127.0.0.1:3191`, flip **局域网访问** on, and confirm the card reports the forwarder listening on the machine's LAN IPv4 at 3191.
2. Open the **loopback** URL (`http://127.0.0.1:3191`) in a browser: the phone icon sits in the sidebar foot; the panel mints a QR whose link is `<lan-url>/pair-accept?pair=<token>`.
3. In a second tab under mobile emulation (390x844, touch) open that link: the chain `/pair-accept → /pair-app?grant=<one-time> → /` on an https origin, ending at `/pair-app` instead over plain-HTTP LAN, sets the device cookie, spends the grant, serves the patched official shell, and boots the UI — `document.body.classList` carries `dsh-remote-portrait`, the adaptation stylesheet and the whale button exist, and `__DSH_TRANSPORT__.ownsHost` is `true`. The settings surface renders host data (host mode), not a memory mirror. In an https deployment the shell also registers the reopen service worker (`/pair-app.sw.js`); reloading `/` in that tab boots the app instead of the harness 401. Over plain-HTTP L
